AI Brief — Thursday, 12 November 2026 (IST) — covering Wednesday 11 November 2026

> Anthropic set a price range for an IPO that could value it at up to $1.4 trillion, Google opened up Gemini 4 Carbon, and China answered with new Baidu, Alibaba and MiniMax models.
> DeepMind used AI to mathematically check Signal's encryption code, while New York opened registration for frontier AI developers.

# WORLD

No confirmed military AI incident (an attack or accident involving AI) in this window. The biggest defence stories were about autonomous weapons and drone security.

### China's GJ-11 combat drone carries out its first live weapons drop
China's air force says its Hongdu GJ-11 uncrewed combat aircraft has made its first live drop of a precision-guided munition and is now in service "at the system level", according to Aviation Week, citing Chinese state media. It's a sign that uncrewed combat aircraft are moving out of testing and into service. Details come from the PLA and have not been independently checked. (Theme: Technology trends)
Source: Aviation Week https://aviationweek.com/defense/budget-policy-operations/hongdu-gj-11-ucav-conducts-first-live-drop-enters-service-plaaf

### Germany reportedly bans Chinese-made drones from military bases
Germany has banned commercially available Chinese-made drones from its military bases and training grounds, effective immediately, over fears they could send sensitive data to Beijing. Der Spiegel first reported this, and The Guardian picked it up. Western militaries are increasingly worried about connected Chinese hardware. (Theme: AI policy and regulation)
Source: The Guardian https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/11/germany-bans-chinese-drones-military-bases-spying-security

# USA

### Anthropic starts its IPO roadshow with a valuation of up to $1.4 trillion
Anthropic has launched the roadshow for its proposed Nasdaq listing under the ticker ANT. It set a price range of $70 to $78 a share for 825 million Class A shares, which would raise up to about $64.4 billion and value the company at up to about $1.404 trillion at the top of the range. The range was filed late on 10 November US time, and the final price is not set yet. (Theme: AI industry and startup news)
Source: Anthropic https://www.anthropic.com/news/roadshow-launch
Also: CNBC https://www.cnbc.com/2026/11/10/anthropic-sets-price-range-of-70-to-78-in-upcoming-ipo.html

### Google makes Gemini 4 Carbon, its strongest model, widely available
Gemini 4 Carbon is now available through the paid Gemini API, Google AI Studio and Gemini for business, and is rolling out to Google AI Ultra subscribers in the Gemini app and AI Mode in Search. Google pitches it at long agent tasks such as complex coding, research and security work. Launch pricing is $2 per million input tokens and $10 per million output tokens. Calling it Google's "strongest" model is the company's own description. (Theme: New AI models and tools)
Source: Google https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/gemini-4-carbon-now-available/

### DeepMind's AlphaProof Code formally verifies parts of Signal's encryption
Google DeepMind used a new AI system, AlphaProof Code, to produce machine-checked Lean proofs of key security properties of Signal's real production code, including forward secrecy and authentication, down to the compiled machine code. The proofs cover specific properties, not every possible attack. The work is a strong sign that AI can make formal software verification practical. (Theme: AI breakthroughs)
Source: Google DeepMind https://deepmind.google/blog/introducing-alphaproof-code/
Also: WIRED https://www.wired.com/story/a-new-ai-tool-from-google-deepmind-formally-verified-the-signal-protocol/

### New York opens frontier AI registration and an AI testing centre
Governor Kathy Hochul opened the state's RAISE Act portal, where large frontier AI developers must register by 1 January 2027. She also launched a research centre at SUNY Binghamton, where researchers will independently test frontier AI systems and develop safety standards. (Theme: AI policy and regulation)
Source: New York State https://www.governor.ny.gov/news/governor-hochul-declares-ny-will-lead-nation-ai-science-and-safety-launches-new-research

# CHINA

### Baidu releases ERNIE 5.5 Flash Preview, with open weights promised
Baidu released ERNIE 5.5 Flash Preview, a mixture-of-experts model with 280 billion total parameters (14 billion active) and a million-token context window, tuned for coding, 3D modelling, knowledge work and video creation. The API is live on Qianfan, and Xinhua reports the weights will be open-sourced on 25 November. Baidu itself calls this an unfinished checkpoint, and its benchmark claims come from the company. (Theme: New AI models and tools)
Source: Baidu https://ernie.baidu.com/release/ernie-5-5-flash-preview/
Also: Xinhua https://www.xinhuanet.com/tech/20261111/183aa161e70b4942b622e10b5e3da605/c.html

### Alibaba opens a preview of Qwen4-Max
Alibaba opened a preview of Qwen4-Max, the flagship of its next Qwen generation. It accepts image and video input and handles up to a million tokens of context. It is available through Alibaba's Token Plan subscription and in the Qwen app, Qoder, QwenWork and QwenStudio. The full Qwen4 launch is still to come. (Theme: New AI models and tools)
Source: TechNode https://technode.com/2026/11/11/alibaba-opens-qwen4-max-preview-with-a-million-token-context-window/

### MiniMax open-sources H3-Image for fast 4K images
MiniMax released H3-Image, an image generation and editing model, with open weights on the evening of 10 November China time. The company says it is 1.5 to 2 times faster than mainstream tools in standard mode and costs about 50% to 70% of their price. Those speed and price figures are company claims. (Theme: New AI models and tools)
Source: The Paper https://www.thepaper.cn/newsDetail_forward_34452449

# ASIA

### Singapore start-up Sapiens says it cuts robot AI training to 30 minutes
Sapiens Technology says it trains only one to three billion parameters of a model instead of the whole thing, which cuts robotics training from weeks or months to as little as 30 minutes. It says it is in talks with more than 30 robotics and medical firms in the US, China and Singapore. These are the company's own claims and have not been independently tested. (Theme: AI breakthroughs)
Source: The Straits Times https://www.straitstimes.com/tech/singapore-start-up-sapiens-cracks-ai-training-bottleneck-makes-waves-overseas

### South Korea jumps to 10th in IMD's digital and AI competitiveness ranking
South Korea's science ministry says the country climbed eight places to 10th of 70 economies in the IMD ranking. The US is first, Singapore second in Asia-Pacific, China seventh and Japan 19th. (Theme: Technology trends)
Source: Yonhap https://en.yna.co.kr/view/AEN20261111002200320

### Dassault Systèmes to set up an ASEAN industrial AI lab in Singapore
Dassault Systèmes signed an MoU with Singapore's Economic Development Board to set up its ASEAN Industrial AI Virtual Twin Lab there. It plans to hire more than 30 AI professionals over five years. (Theme: AI industry and startup news)
Source: TNGlobal https://technode.global/2026/11/11/frances-dassault-systemes-to-set-up-asean-industrial-ai-virtual-twin-lab-in-singapore/

# INDIA

### Andhra Pradesh clears a Rs 31,387 crore AI data centre near Visakhapatnam
The Andhra Pradesh Cabinet approved a 512 MW green AI data centre by AM Intelligence at Bheemunipatnam, worth Rs 31,387 crore. It also cleared land at Bhogapuram for Reliance's giga-scale AI data centre and a Rs 570 crore Epack plant that will make AI data centre equipment. (Theme: AI industry and startup news)
Source: The New Indian Express https://www.newindianexpress.com/states/andhra-pradesh/2026/Nov/11/ap-cabinet-clears-rs-313k-crore-ai-data-centre-at-bhimili

### YoLearn.ai launches Pragya, a K-12 tutoring LLM built on NEP 2020
YoLearn.ai launched Pragya, a model fine-tuned on CBSE curriculum data for tutoring in more than 12 Indian languages. It will power the company's tutor in its 20,000 partner schools. The claim that it is "India's first" such model and its teacher-panel scores come from the company, and the article is a sponsored "Spotlight" piece. (Theme: New AI models and tools)
Source: The Times of India https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/education/yolearn-ai-launches-pragya-indias-first-llm-for-k-12-built-on-nep-2020-and-ncf-2023/articleshow/135733251.cms

### BCG ranks India an AI "Rising Contender", powered by talent rather than compute
BCG's AI Maturity Matrix 2026, which covers more than 75 economies, puts India in the second of four readiness tiers. That is below the seven "AI Pioneers", including the US, China and Japan. BCG says India's strength is its large pool of AI specialists and IT-services workers. (Theme: Technology trends)
Source: Mint (PTI) https://www.livemint.com/technology/india-ranked-an-ai-rising-contender-by-bcg-built-on-talent-rather-than-compute-11794397321852.html

